  "title": "Things Fall Apart (Chinua Achebe)",
  "summary": "Chinua Achebe’s novel Things Fall Apart, set in late 19th-century Nigeria, was published in London by William Heinemann on 17 June 1958 after the manuscript, completed in Nigeria, was sent to British publishers. Its success launched Heinemann’s African Writers Series, of which it was the first title and Achebe the first advisory editor.",
